  "conclusions": [
    "1. Goldilocks zone exists for all L1-L5: too-low SFT -> all-zero GRPO groups, too-high SFT -> all-one groups (no variance -> no signal)",
    "2. L1 Goldilocks zone: [0.200, 0.480], peak at 0.340",
    "3. Optimal SFT starting quality for RL: 0.35 (maximizes RL improvement = +0.423)",
    "4. Temperature 0.7 provides good signal (learnable >0.95)",
    "5. SFT overfitting (pass>0.90) causes GRPO collapse: all-one rate >50%",
    "6. Cross-level transfer: L1->L3 coefficient ~0.5; SFT must reach L1>=0.60 to make L3 bootstrappable",
    "7. Pre-registered criteria: 4 red flags, 4 secondary checks",
    "8. The SFT-to-RL bridge is the highest-risk transition; pre-registration prevents post-hoc rationalization"
  ],
